{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217488","model_call":22,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"spotlight effect\" \"everyone is watching\" (+ self-conscious overestimate attention))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"spotlight effect\" \"everyone is watching\" (+ self-conscious overestimate attention))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1526547997#6_3237839821","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3757","rank":1,"snippet":"a person moves from one room to the next, the brain works as a file that retrieves all information about the current room and the events that occurred in it. When a person goes to another room, the focus shifts to the new, current room. The person has trouble recalling what they had intended to do in the now, current room making it hard for a person to recall the task thought of in the prior room. You can overcome this phenomenon by mumbling the task as you move from one room to another. ( source) 3. <cover>Spotlight Effect: a phenomenon that makes people significantly overestimate how noticeable their embarrassing behaviors are to others. This effect occurs due to cognitive bias. Share Share on Pinterest Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Have you ever walked into a room and felt like everyone is watching </cover>and judging you? If you have felt that way, you have experienced the “spotlight effect.”\" , \"start_char\": 3395.000000 , \"title\": \"10 Psychological Phenomena we Might have Experienced\" , \"url\": \"https://unbelievable-facts.com/2019/02/psychological-phenomena.html\" }"},"time":54},"model_calls":22,"document_judgments":18,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
