{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217488","model_call":36,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3765"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3765"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#12_2614812616","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3765","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1689181162#12_2614812616\" , \"end_char\": 6914.000000 , \"headings\": \"What Is the Difference Between Paranoia and Reasonable Suspicion? What Is the Difference Between Paranoia and Reasonable Suspicion? What Is Paranoia? Delusional vs. Reasonable Paranoia Schizophrenia Symptoms: The Link to <cover>Paranoia and Anxiety When to Seek Treatment for Anxiety About Being Watched References: Tonycliftontaxi Jonh Jo \" , \"segment\": \"A person with schizophrenia might try to contact a celebrity to warn them of a threat or reach out to a lawyer to report government surveillance that doesn’t seem to be happening. When to Seek Treatment for Anxiety About Being Watched Mental health </cover>treatment can help anyone experiencing anxiety, whether their anxiety is rooted in a real source or the product of a mental health diagnosis. Activists such as lawyers or protest leaders who have reasonable fears about being monitored may find therapy helps them manage their anxiety, deal with the effects of those fears on their relationships, and separate reasonable fears from unreasonable ones. People who have a condition linked to unreasonable paranoia may "},"time":9},"model_calls":36,"document_judgments":32,"relevance_3":16,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
